Superweapon targeting cursors: arming exclusion, Esc cancel, neutral no-type cursor.

Audit of the SW arming flow vs retail (all 12 ConvertAction cursor ids were
already correct and tested): three gaps fixed, no save-format change.

- arm_superweapon(type,phase) is refused while a placement is pending and
  reports success (placement wins, the set_mode_ rule); begin_placement
  disarms SW targeting, so a map click can no longer fire an SW while a
  placement ghost is up. w2_arm_sw latches nothing and stays silent when
  refused.
- Esc/F10 in game runs the cancel chain first: an armed SW (or other mode)
  is disarmed, dropping the latched type and any Chronosphere source pick
  (w2_disarm_sw); the options menu opens only when nothing was pending.
  Before, Esc left the SW armed behind the menu.
- superweapon_cursor(None) is the neutral Default cursor, not Nuke.

Right-click cancel, the Chronosphere two-click destination phase, the
radar_order/minimap commit path and Action::SuperWeapon in action_at were
audited and behave per retail; they are locked in by the new tests.
Tests: 4 asset-free cases in test_input.cpp (arm/type/phase/action,
exclusion both ways, right-click + Esc-chain cancel without firing,
radar_order commit) + the None cursor id in test_superweapon.cpp.

